From 79a80f69261dee0f5b61c225d489e38294400c7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: devbotbo <7118.eth@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 20:59:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Test verifier mode end to end over the real router

Create a request with the bridge's nonce, read the signed request object back
the way a wallet does and check it carries that nonce and the service's own
encryption key, then answer it like a wallet: mint a fresh SD-JWT VC
presentation (self-signed issuer leaf in x5c, KB-JWT bound to the request's
nonce and client_id at the current time), encrypt it to the advertised key and
POST the form. GET /result/:id must return the exact presentation string.

Also covered: pending before the response, 409 on a nonce that is still in
flight and its release after a verified or rejected outcome, rejection with the
error text, the RESULT_INCLUDES_PRESENTATION=false shape, and that a
landing-page session is not pending here but its outcome is served.

josekit joins the dev-dependencies for the encrypt half (verifier-core only
decrypts).
